From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BDK Patches <patches@bdk.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bdk: link //bdk into the Mac framework

BDK keeps its engine code in the //bdk overlay (chromium/bdk in the BDK
repository), which is mounted at src/bdk. Nothing in upstream depends on
it, so GN would never build it. Add //bdk to the public_deps of
chrome_framework so the overlay is compiled and linked into the framework
that BDK ships as its runtime.

Also export bdk_overlay_marker() from the framework. The framework hides
every symbol that is not in framework.exports, and the BDK build runs nm on
the framework to check that //bdk was really linked in.

Used by: the BDK engine (//bdk), checked by the chromium:build target.
---
 chrome/BUILD.gn              | 7 ++++++-
 chrome/app/framework.exports | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/BUILD.gn b/chrome/BUILD.gn
index 06bfcf5a90d093b9ac8e255e93ef2ffd0a00421e..1ece07fef574d21cf4c2191270a76282c96ffb5b 100644
--- a/chrome/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/BUILD.gn
@@ -1398,7 +1398,12 @@ if (is_win) {
       "CHROMIUM_SHORT_NAME=$chrome_product_short_name",
     ]
 
-    public_deps = [ ":chrome_dll" ]
+    public_deps = [
+      ":chrome_dll",
+
+      # BDK: the engine overlay. See chromium/patches in the BDK repository.
+      "//bdk",
+    ]
 
     bundle_deps = [
       ":aperitif_library",
diff --git a/chrome/app/framework.exports b/chrome/app/framework.exports
index 37c881f5d29511347ce508ce7bfb1f54cb37a120..3ad0d19a0c1debfe3cc7180c8d02a2a7930b7dcd 100644
--- a/chrome/app/framework.exports
+++ b/chrome/app/framework.exports
@@ -19,3 +19,4 @@
 _ChromeAppModeStart_v8
 _ChromeMain
 _ChromeWebAppShortcutCopierMain
+_bdk_overlay_marker
